  "title": "Four Shelf Zero Totals",
  "description": "## Task\n\nA store has four shelves, each with a list of price adjustments. A pick takes exactly one adjustment from each shelf, identified by its position. Count the picks whose four adjustments add up to zero.\n\n## Input\n\n- `a`, `b`, `c`, `d` — four lists of integers, all of the same length.\n\n## Output\n\nThe number of index quadruples `(i, j, k, l)` with `a[i] + b[j] + c[k] + d[l] == 0`.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\nzero_total_picks([1, 2], [-2, -1], [-1, 2], [0, 2])  # returns 2\nzero_total_picks([0], [0], [0], [0])  # returns 1\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 0 ≤ length of each list ≤ 400\n- -10^6 ≤ each value ≤ 10^6\n- Trying every quadruple would be too slow for the largest inputs.\n",
  "signature": "def zero_total_picks(a: list[int], b: list[int], c: list[int], d: list[int]) -> int",
  "topic": "meet in the middle",
  "difficulty": "medium",
